; A hardware register is where the hardware puts it, so `.mmio` needs the address. Without one it
; would be data the program lays out, which a register never is.
.module main
.cpu 6502

.segment BSS
.mmio LATCH: .byte                  ;! error[mmio-needs-an-address]: `.mmio` declares a hardware register at the address the hardware gives it: write `.mmio LATCH: .byte = $address`
